        "category": null,
        "deathNote": false,
        "description": {
          "gm": "<p>If the players successfully use the B.F.C. on the colossus, be sure to inform them that it's now possible to climb it, and that it would give them easier access to attacking the zombie's heart.</p>",
          "value": "<p>The zombie colossus is so massive and its flesh is so dense that it is immune to all damage. If the zombie colossus is targeted with a Strike from a hacked B.F.C., the Strike automatically succeeds, the colossus loses its immunity to damage, and the hacked B.F.C. is destroyed after the Strike resolves.</p>\n<p>The impact from the weapon ruptures the colossus's body; new scars and protruding bones can be used as handholds for climbing creatures. A creature who spends two actions and succeeds at a @Check[type:athletics|dc:18] check can climb to a position that allows them to access the colossus's heart. The zombie colossus has weakness 13 to all damage from creatures in this position.</p>\n<p>The zombie colossus can remove a climbing creature by using the Shove action (or by hitting with Slab of Flesh and using the Improved Push ability). Creatures who are pushed off of the zombie colossus fall 20 ft.</p>"
        },
